# RONDB-1062: deterministic scan<->scan deadlock (testDeadlock -scan s).
# Two exclusive ordered index scans (ascending/descending, batch 2) on a
# single-fragment table run concurrently.  A DBTUX error insert (12010)
# makes each scan stall after locking its first row until the program
# clears it, so both still hold a row when they collide on each other's,
# forming a scan<->scan cycle.  With TransactionDeadlockDetectionTimeout
# = 60s (see .cnf), the program asserts the cycle is resolved in well
# under that (one scan aborted with a lock-wait/timeout error, the other
# survives) - which proves proactive detection.  The program's exit code
# is the pass/fail signal; its output is logged to NDB_TOOLS_OUTPUT, not
# the result file.
# scan<->scan deadlock detected and resolved proactively.
